EntranceLocked [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Locks the entrance of Lane A/B of the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path> (true) or nor (false). It thus
prevents that Transporters can enter the object.
Remarks
The TwoLaneTrack will finish transporting the Transporters already located on it.
It does not accept any additional Transporters and enters them into the Blocking List of Lane A/B.
• If the Transporter wants to enter the TwoLaneTrack at its entrance, the Transporter is entered into the
Forward Blocking List of Lane A/B.
• If the Transporter is moving backward and wants to enter a length-oriented object at its exit, the
Transporter is entered into the Exit Blocking List of Lane A/B.
The TwoLaneTrack starts transporting again, when you set the attribute to false. The first Transporter in
the Forward Blocking List of Lane A/B is going to be moved on first.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.A.EntranceLocked:boolean
<Path>.B.EntranceLocked:boolean
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyTwoLaneTrack.B.EntranceLocked := true
waituntil MyTwoLaneTrack.B.NumMu 10 prio 1
MyTwoLaneTrack.B.EntranceLocked := false
EntranceLocked [SimTalk] - lane A or B
11-2544 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

