ExitLocked [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Locks the exit of Lane A/B of the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path> (true) or not (false). It thus
prevents that Transporters leave the object.
Remarks
The TwoLaneTrack does not transport the Transporters to the successor in the material flow, but enters
them into the Exit Blocking List of Lane A/B of the TwoLaneTrack.
Once the exit is unlocked again, the TwoLaneTrack moves the first Transporter in the Exit Blocking List of
Lane A/B on to its successor.
When setting ExitLocked to false Transporters entered into the Exit Blocking List will make another
attempt to exit the TwoLaneTrack.
Note
The Transporter does not trigger the Exit Control if you set ExitLocked to true.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.A.ExitLocked:boolean
<Path>.B.ExitLocked:boolean
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyTwoLaneTrack.A.ExitLocked := true
See also
Exit Locked [lane A]
ExitLocked [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Plant Simulation Help 11-2549
