PullCtrl [SimTalk] - lane A or B
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Method when the TwoLaneTrack designated by <Path> is ready to accept a new
Transporter on the specified lane or when it is ready, when a new Transporter is Waiting at its entrance.
In the Pull Control you can determine which Transporter, which intends to move onto the TwoLaneTrack,
the TwoLaneTrack will accept. For this you have to get the Forward Blocking List of the respective lane
with the method fwBlockList and unblock a Transporter in the list with the method unblock.
Note
If you only need the first entry of the Forward Blocking List, use the read-only-attribute
FwBlockListEntry1 for those objects which have a Forward Blocking List. Access is much faster than
with the method fwBlockList.
Suppose that red parts are especially important and thus have to be processed first. You can always pull red
parts from the predecessors in the Pull Control first and then parts with other colors.
Note
The Pull Control does not determine if a Transporter is to be moved on to this successor or to another
successor, but it selects one of the Transporters which already decided to move to this successor.
Note
For the TwoLaneTrack the Pull Control only applies to Transporters that drive forward, meaning that
they enter the TwoLaneTrack at the entrance and they exit at the exit. It does not apply to Transporters
driving in reverse entering at the exit and not to Transporters that have been moved to a certain
position.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.A.PullCtrl:method
<Path>.B.PullCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
PullCtrl [SimTalk] - lane A or B
11-2552 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
MyTwoLaneTrack.A.PullCtrl := &MyPullMethod
